  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "A cell phone plan costs \\(\\$20\\) each month, plus \\(5\\)¢ per text message sent, plus \\(10\\)¢ for each minute used over \\(30\\) hours. In January Michelle sent \\(100\\) text messages and talked for \\(30.5\\) hours. How much did she have to pay?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\$24.00\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\$24.50\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\$25.50\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\$28.00\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\$30.00\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Only the time beyond \\(30\\) hours incurs the extra minute charge. Michelle's excess time is\n\\[\n30.5-30=0.5\\text{ hour}=30\\text{ minutes}.\n\\]\nHer \\(100\\) text messages cost \\(100\\times\\$0.05=\\$5\\), and the excess calls cost \\(30\\times\\$0.10=\\$3\\). Adding these to the monthly charge gives\n\\[\n\\$20+\\$5+\\$3=\\boxed{\\$28.00}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
